  Boots are the last armor type you want to enchant.  Mostly 
because of the many types of magic boots:  stealth, water 
walking, levitation, jumping, speed, etc.  If you need to switch
to the levitation boots to cross water or on the Plane of Air,
you don't want to lose AC when doing so.

From <http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/abil-343.txt>:
Class- and race-dependent abilities and gained intrinsics
"Valkyrie
~~~~~~~~
XL 1 : Cold resistance
XL 1 : Stealth
XL 7 : Speed"


  So you won't need stealth (unless a gremlin steals it.)  Speed
you've already got, i.e. you're "fast".  The "very fast" from 
speed boots is only 25% faster than "fast."  Don't get me wrong,
that's nice to have.  But sometimes levitation, jumping, or water
walking will be (briefly) better to have.

  And there's no other way to walk on water/lava than (fireproof)
boots of water walking.  This can be a lifesaver in a level with 
both ice squares and firetraps.  (Beats an amulet of lifesaving 
all hollow.)

  Also, jumping boots let you travel over twice as fast on the 
plane of fire and the Astral Plane.  Few monsters are a threat
when they're receding rapidly in your rear-view mirror.  (On my
first ascension I #jumped past Pestilence twice, without being 
touched either time.)  Cast spell of haste self or save some 
blessed potions of speed and you can still be "very fast".


  And the spell of haste self can be cast "off-line", when you're
not in trouble, i.e. wearing your best spell-casting armor after
dropping the amulet of yendor.  The spell of haste self can also 
be pumped up considerably.  Valkyries can get to basic in the 
escaped spell school.


From <http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/spl1-343.txt>:

"...each attempt to cast a spell drains energy equal to 5 times 
the spell's level (randomly up to three times this amount if you 
have the Amulet) for a successful casting, or half as much for a 
failure.  (See hppw-343.txt for details of how fast you will 
regain this energy.)  Your hunger increases by twice the amount 
of energy that would be drained for a success regardless, but
it will not make you faint. "


  Haste Self is a level 3 spell.



  Also you'll find a lot of boots in the dungeon, some of 
which will already be well enchanted.  In my current game I'm 
wearing +3 blessed low boots, which were found that way.  I've 
also got a couple of pair of +2 dwarven boots, but the low boots 
are lighter.  (I'm using the spell of haste self to be "very 
fast.")  That extra three points of AC is the best I could have
hoped for from a blessed scroll of enchant armor.


  Save your first scroll of enchant armor for making dragon scale
mail.  It would be a shame to waste a wish for Gray/Silver DSM if
it gets handed to you.  (Either through luck or wand/spell of 
turn undead.)


  Then enchant a shirt: 
    1) Shirt's have zero base AC
    2) You're unlikely to find a highly enchanted shirt in the 
       Dungeons.
    3) There are no magic types of shirts.


